# Regenerate-first with a remote plugin: the template switches to the local
# plugin, and the steps install it before buf generate.
stubs v1generic
exec migrate
cmp stdout out.txt
stdout 'has no v2 release yet'
stdout 'go install connectrpc.com/connect/v2/cmd/protoc-gen-connect-go@latest'
stdout 'no Go source changes are proposed yet'
stdout 'Proposed Buf template updates'
stdout 'no Go source changes are proposed yet'
exec go build ./...
-- service.go --
package app

import (
	"context"

	"connectrpc.com/connect"
	pingv1 "example.com/app/gen/connect/ping/v1"
	"example.com/app/gen/connect/ping/v1/pingv1connect"
)

type pingServer struct {
	pingv1connect.UnimplementedPingServiceHandler
}

func (s *pingServer) Ping(ctx context.Context, req *connect.Request[pingv1.PingRequest]) (*connect.Response[pingv1.PingResponse], error) {
	return connect.NewResponse(&pingv1.PingResponse{Number: req.Msg.Number, Text: req.Msg.Text}), nil
}
-- buf.gen.yaml --
version: v2
plugins:
  - remote: buf.build/connectrpc/go:v1.18.1
    out: gen
-- out.txt --
Scanned 1 Go file and 1 Buf template. The generated Connect code still targets
v1, so no Go source changes are proposed yet.

Generated v1 Connect code:
  ./gen/connect/ping/v1/pingv1connect

Proposed Buf template updates (rerun with -w to apply):
  ./buf.gen.yaml: bufgen_remote_to_local=1
--- ./buf.gen.yaml
+++ ./buf.gen.yaml
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 version: v2
 plugins:
-  - remote: buf.build/connectrpc/go:v1.18.1
+  - local: protoc-gen-connect-go
     out: gen
 


The following issues require a manual update:
  ./buf.gen.yaml:3:1: buf.build/connectrpc/go:v1.18.1 has no v2 release yet, so this entry now runs the local plugin. Install it with `go install connectrpc.com/connect/v2/cmd/protoc-gen-connect-go@latest`, and switch back to the remote plugin once connect-go v2.0.0 is released.

First, move the dependencies and generated code to v2:

  1. connect-go-v2-migrate -w  (applies the Buf template update above)
  2. go get -u \
       connectrpc.com/connect/v2
     (pulls the v2 core and ecosystem modules into go.mod)
  3. go install connectrpc.com/connect/v2/cmd/protoc-gen-connect-go@latest
     (./buf.gen.yaml runs the local protoc-gen-connect-go binary. v1 and v2
     share the binary name, so reinstalling from the /v2 module switches
     generation to v2)
  4. buf generate

Then re-run connect-go-v2-migrate to work through the Go source changes: it
rewrites the call sites against the v2 stubs and reports anything that needs
a manual update.

Full migration guide: https://github.com/connectrpc/connect-go/blob/main/docs/v2-migration.md
